<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoruba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yoruba people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yoruba are a major West African people of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, with a long tradition of urban city-states and the sacred city of Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> was the most powerful Yoruba state, dominating the region from the seventeenth to the early nineteenth century. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>'s expansion contributed to the collapse of Oyo and to prolonged wars among the Yoruba states.</p></div>
